    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated for a woman of 42 on immunotherapy for rectal cancer. Breast screening is due under the current recommendation to screen every two years from 40; a mammogram was ordered. Cervical screening is up to date. Hepatitis B surface antibody was negative before treatment, so the two-dose adjuvanted hepatitis B vaccine was started today; inactivated vaccines are safe on PD-1 blockade. Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines are due when this season&apos;s vaccines arrive. Sun protection was discussed in detail because she is outdoors all day. [S]<list><item>Hepatitis B vaccine dose 1 today; dose 2 at cycle 9.</item><item>Screening mammogram ordered.</item><item>Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines in the autumn.</item><item>Broad-spectrum sunscreen of SPF 30 or more, reapplied every two hours on the course, with a wide-brimmed hat and sun sleeves.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Immune-related hypothyroidism on levothyroxine (E03.2)</content>. TSH 3.1 mIU/L and free T4 1.1 ng/dL six weeks after starting levothyroxine 75 micrograms: replaced, and symptoms gone. [S]<list><item>Continue levothyroxine 75 micrograms on waking, four hours from iron.</item><item>TSH and free T4 every six weeks while on dostarlimab.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Mismatch repair-deficient low rectal cancer on dostarlimab (C20)</content>. Near-complete response at three months; cycle 7 today. [S]<list><item>Cycles 8 and 9 as booked; final restaging after cycle 9.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>112/68 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 score 2; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>One or two drinks a month</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Intimate partner violence screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Negative; she feels safe</td></tr><tr><td>Breast cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Mammogram every two years from 40; first screening mammogram ordered</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>HPV and cytology co-test two years ago, normal; next in three years</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Screening does not apply: she is under cancer surveillance with MRI, endoscopy and colonoscopy</td></tr><tr><td>HIV, hepatitis B and hepatitis C screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>All negative before treatment; hepatitis B surface antibody negative</td></tr><tr><td>Prediabetes and diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>BMI 22.5 with no other risk factor; fasting glucose normal before each cycle</td></tr><tr><td>Lipid screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Lipid panel three years ago normal</td></tr><tr><td>Skin cancer prevention counseling</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Sun protection for an outdoor athlete; skin examined, no suspicious lesion</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dose 1 of the two-dose adjuvanted series; dose 2 in one month or later</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>When this season&apos;s vaccine is available</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>This season&apos;s vaccine in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap five years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended from 50, or from 19 for immunosuppression; PD-1 blockade alone is not immunosuppressive treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Contraception counseling</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Levonorgestrel IUD continued during treatment and for at least four months after the last dose</td></tr><tr><td>Dental and vision examination</td><td>Due</td><td>Dental cleaning due; eye examination next year</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Hepatitis B vaccine (adjuvanted, two-dose series), dose 1 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Schneider BJ, et al. Management of Immune-Related Adverse Events in Patients Treated With Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Therapy: ASCO Guideline Update. J Clin Oncol 2021;39(36):4073-4126 (PMID 34724392) (2021); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Breast Cancer: Screening (2024); Cervical Cancer: Screening (2018); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Cycle 7 today; cycles 8 and 9 as booked; hepatitis B dose 2 at cycle 9; mammogram; final restaging after cycle 9. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-05: after nine doses: final restaging, clinical complete response, and the watch-and-wait surveillance plan. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
