    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 20 minutes, with her consent. She named a health care agent, recorded in the confidential part of the chart and not named here, and completed a health care proxy form. She said that she wants every treatment with a real chance of controlling the cancer, including surgery and a colostomy if the tumor ever regrows, and wants to be told the facts at once and in plain words. If she were ever too ill to decide and unlikely to recover, she would want care aimed at comfort, with her pain fully treated. To be revisited at each change in her health and at least yearly. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
